(Chapter 9: The Citric Acid Cycle and Oxidative Phosphorylation) '
(Substrate-Level vs Oxidative Phosphorylation) '
(1. Pyruvate dehydrogenase complex converts pyruvate to Acetyl-CoA in the mitochondrial matrix.) '
(2. Citric Acid Cycle produces 3 NADH, 1 FADH2, and 1 GTP \(ATP equivalent\) per acetyl-CoA.) '
(3. High-energy electron carriers feed into Electron Transport Chain Complexes I-IV.) '
