(Chapter 9, Section 4: Chemiosmotic Coupling & ATP Synthase) '
(Peter Mitchell Chemiosmotic Hypothesis \(Nobel Prize in Chemistry 1978\)) '
(Protons pumped across the inner mitochondrial membrane establish an electrochemical proton gradient \(pmf\).) '
(The F0 rotor subunit rotates as protons flow down the electrochemical gradient, mechanically driving ATP synthesis in catalytic F1 domain.) '
(Total theoretical yield: 30 to 32 ATP molecules per oxidized glucose molecule.) '
ET
